+    // The lock surface starts wholly invisible: background.opacity is 0, and so
+    // are scale and opacity on both lockContent and content. Nothing but
+    // initAnim below ever makes them appear. That is fine when the lock is
+    // asked for by hand, and it is not fine when lockBeforeSleep asks for it —
+    // the surface is then created inside the PrepareForSleep transition, the
+    // animation starts, and the machine suspends before the compositor has
+    // presented a single frame. Qt advances animations off frame callbacks, so
+    // nothing moves while suspended and the animation comes back from resume
+    // still sitting at zero. What that looks like is a lock screen with a
+    // background and no password field — and it still takes keys, so the dots
+    // it would draw for them are invisible too, which is the part that makes it
+    // read as frozen rather than as broken.
+    //
+    // complete() jumps to the end state instead of restarting: after a resume
+    // the entrance flourish is not what anyone is waiting for, and on an
+    // animation that already finished it is a no-op.
+    Connections {
+        function onResumed(): void {
+            if (root.lock.locked && !root.unlocking)
+                initAnim.complete();
+        }
+
+        target: SessionManager
+    }
+
     SequentialAnimation {
         id: unlockAnim
 
